<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">A new TTI bridge &middot; exact sum, physical proposal, explicit debt</p>
  <h1>When Differentials Accumulate</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">Could accumulated differentials appear physically as mass, and could their
    distribution then contribute to gravity? Calculus permits the accumulation. Physics requires much more.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">Three statements, only one conjectural bridge</p>
    <h2 id="t-three-levels">Do Not Skip the Middle</h2>
    <p><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>Mathematics:</strong> an integral accumulates differential
      contributions into a finite quantity, and a discrete sum accumulates increments.</p>
    <p><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>Established physics:</strong> mass&ndash;energy and momentum enter
      the stress&ndash;energy tensor; in general relativity that tensor sources spacetime curvature.</p>
    <p><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> <strong>TTI bridge:</strong> suppose a covariantly defined integration
      deposit contributes an additional stress&ndash;energy component. That is a model proposal, not a consequence
      of writing \(dx\), a Fibonacci sum or an integral sign.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap reveal">
  <div class="grid two">
    <article class="frame card">
      <p class="kicker">Established mathematics <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h2 id="t-calculus">A Differential Is Not a Grain of Stuff</h2>
      <p class="formula">\[F(b)-F(a)=\int_a^b F'(x)\,dx.\]</p>
      <p>In standard analysis, \(dx\) participates in a limiting construction, differential form or measure.
        It is not automatically a smallest physical length, elapsed moment or packet of matter. TTI&rsquo;s
        <a href="/dx/">completed smallest gathering</a> is a metaphysical interpretation laid over this
        mathematics.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card">
      <p class="kicker">Established relativity <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h2 id="t-einstein">What Curves Spacetime</h2>
      <p class="formula">\[G_{\mu\nu}+\Lambda g_{\mu\nu}=
        \frac{8\pi G}{c^4}T_{\mu\nu}.\]</p>
      <p>Rest mass is not gravity&rsquo;s only source. Energy density, momentum density, pressure and stress all
        enter \(T_{\mu\nu}\). Most ordinary visible mass also does not come directly from the Higgs field;
        much of proton and neutron mass is QCD binding and kinetic energy.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

